From b2dc128264a937e260cf07b3de7989a168580bdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex Unleashed <codex-unleashed@holdmyspot.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:46:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add Codex Unleashed branding and build metadata

Identify the unofficial fork in the welcome screen and /status. Keep the
OpenAI Codex title in /status, align its fork label and project URL with the
title text, and retain the complete URL when it wraps on narrow terminals.
Share the fork notice renderer between the two headers.

TDD for /status against rust-v0.159.2 (ff6aec96948b70d94983af2641a6b67c94faeff5):
RED: apply the existing branding patch, add the rendered-header assertion,
and run from codex-rs:
  CODEX_UNLEASHED_BUILD_NUMBER=15 cargo +1.95.0 test -p codex-tui --lib status_snapshot_includes_reasoning_details
Result: 0 passed, 1 failed at the missing fork label and URL assertion.

GREEN with the accompanying snapshot expectations patch, from codex-rs:
  RUST_MIN_STACK=16777216 CODEX_UNLEASHED_BUILD_NUMBER=15 INSTA_UPDATE=no cargo +1.95.0 test -p codex-tui --lib status::tests::
Result: 50 passed, including the exact header and full URL at widths 20/40/80.
  RUST_MIN_STACK=16777216 CODEX_UNLEASHED_BUILD_NUMBER=15 INSTA_UPDATE=no cargo +1.95.0 test -p codex-tui --lib session_header_
Result: 11 passed.
  cargo +1.95.0 fmt --package codex-cli --package codex-tui -- --check
Result: passed.

The initial local Rust 1.98 command fails before testing in unchanged
codex-chatgpt code with a query-depth overflow. The same check with upstream's
Rust 1.95 compiles and reaches the expected behavioral failure. The broader
status suite needs the test-thread stack setting above. No upstream source
is changed to accommodate either environmental failure.
